1
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,600
ANIMAL FEED FOR SALE

2
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,520
If you haven't ordered
your mineral salt blocks yet, hurry up!

3
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,320
The flash sale is almost over, everyone.

4
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,400
Normally, 800 baht a case,

5
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:38,280
but today they're only 700 baht!

6
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,920
Come on, get your orders in!

7
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,960
These mineral salt blocks provide
essential minerals for cows and buffaloes,

8
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:47,840
like sodium and calcium.
They also boost the immune system

9
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,640
and support reproductive health.
And most importantly,

10
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:54,160
the mineral salt blocks
from Chettha Kaset Farm are smooth, dense,

11
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:57,120
and don't crack easily. Right, Hom Ngern?

12
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,280
"That's right! I love them!"

13
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,560
Get your orders in now!
Cows and buffaloes absolutely love them.

14
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,800
Let's see. Kaew wants two cases.

15
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,680
Wow! Thank you so much, Kaew!

16
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:14,760
Wow! You sold 20 cases in just one hour.

17
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,640
That's more than
last week's in-store sales.

18
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:21,160
Ming, you were brilliant
for coming up with this idea.

19
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,320
Auem's great at selling too.
Don't you think, Dad?

20
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,520
I'm so happy.

21
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:36,240
I'll give you and Uncle Tik
a share of today's livestream earnings.

22
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,120
Oh, you don't need to give us a share.

23
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:42,920
Uncle Tik and I talked it over.
Any job that you and Hom Ngern

24
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,080
do without our help,
you can keep all the money.

25
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:52,120
There's a buffalo competition
in Ban Chiang in two months.

26
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,040
I'm thinking of entering Phet Kla

27
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,320
to give our farm more exposure.
Sound good?

28
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,560
Sounds good, Din.

29
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,960
Let's visit Uncle Tik this weekend

30
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,960
so we can start planning
for the competition.

31
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,800
-Sounds good.
-Whoa.

32
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:07,640
You've got your supermarket job,
product reviews, and videos to film.

33
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:10,640
Aren't you working a little too hard
to make money, Auem?

34
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,360
I just want to get Hom Thong back soon.

35
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:16,640
And I want to get Dad's
buffalo conservation center started too.

36
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,000
I'm going to make sure this center

37
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,720
can support our whole family.

38
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,240
You can do it.

39
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,240
That's the spirit.

40
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,000
When are you going
to deal with Auem, Ming?

41
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:37,680
Let her keep selling for a while.
That way, no one will suspect anything.

42
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,480
-Almost done?
-We've got loads today.

43
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,680
-I've got more too!
-Yeah.

44
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:59,840
-Just wait till lunch. You'll see.
-Almost lunchtime?

45
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,160
If that's not enough, there's more.

46
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:04,440
Oh, here they come!

47
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,760
-Here they come.
-Come on, kids! Come on over!

48
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,480
-Fresh handmade meatballs!
-Fresh handmade meatballs, kids!

49
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,960
Fresh meatballs, rolled by hand!

50
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,720
That's right.

51
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,800
Easy, everyone. Line up!

52
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,880
No pushing! Get in line, kids.
There's enough for everyone.

53
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,720
Whoa!

54
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,320
Oh, no!

55
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,440
Oh, no!

56
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,920
Oh my God!

57
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,360
Ugh!

58
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:40,000
I've had enough!
I'm getting the principal over here

59
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:43,560
to see how much trouble
your stall is causing me.

60
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:46,280
And you're selling spicy meatball salad,
just like me.

61
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:50,040
-How? She sells handmade meatballs.
-Exactly.

62
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:53,520
How is that seafood dipping sauce
any different from spicy salad dressing?

63
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:57,840
Sa-Ang, you were doing fine
selling rice dishes.

64
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,600
Why steal my customers too?

65
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:02,560
Hey, if your food was actually good,

66
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,640
no one could steal your customers.

67
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,600
-So your food's that good, huh?
-Hey!

68
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,600
-Hey, wait!
-Don't!

69
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,360
-Calm down!
-I said let go!

70
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:15,040
Mom! Stop it!

71
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:15,960
That's enough!

72
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,320
-Stop!
-Mom!

73
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:26,000
-Mom!
-Oh, no.

74
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:41,720
Orn, how's Mom?

75
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:44,280
Didn't I tell you Mom shouldn't sell here?

76
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:46,280
See? Now look what's happened.

77
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,720
Hello. I'm Auemdao, Sa-Ing's daughter.

78
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:05,920
The parents of the student who got scalded
are sitting right here.

79
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,480
You need to compensate them.

80
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,680
-If we have to pay, so do you!
-Yeah.

81
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:14,000
You tried to grab the pot from my sister.

82
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:17,440
What? Your sister was the one
who dropped the pot.

83
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,920
I've got proof. I have a video.
Here, look.

84
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,240
Here you go.

85
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,080
But you tried to grab my pot first.

86
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,800
Look! My clothes are covered in sauce.

87
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,200
-Everyone saw what happened!
-How can you say that?

88
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:43,000
-Come on.
-Everyone!

89
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,160
-Everyone!
-You grabbed it first!

90
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,840
-Please stop arguing.
-You wouldn't let it go.

91
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,360
I'll pay the compensation myself.

92
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,320
Auem!

93
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:54,200
Principal, according to school rules,

94
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,560
stalls aren't allowed to sell
the same food.

95
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:59,960
I've been selling
spicy meatball salad for ages.

96
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:02,000
You have to get rid of her stall.

97
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,400
-Whoa!
-Otherwise,

98
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,720
I'll sue the school
for breach of contract.

99
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,480
-Is everything settled now?
-Yes.

100
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,160
Thank you.

101
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,200
MONEY TO BUY BACK HOM THONG
-12,000 = 552,000

102
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,400
Why bother picking it up?
Just leave it there.

103
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,720
Throw the meatballs away!

104
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,720
We can't, Mom. They're still good.
We can sell them elsewhere.

105
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,560
I'm not selling anywhere!

106
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:46,800
What? You're quitting
over one little incident?

107
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,600
There are plenty of other places to sell.

108
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:53,240
There's a market outside the supermarket
where Auem works.

109
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,720
I'll book us a spot there.

110
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:57,360
Hey, I said I'm not selling! I'm not!

111
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,160
If you want to sell, do it yourself.

112
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:03,240
What? You're just going to let
your daughter earn all the money?

113
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:06,440
When Yod was around,
he earned enough to support me.

114
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,160
Auem can do the same.

115
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:10,600
-Sa-Ing! Where are you going?
-Aunt.

116
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,560
Don't bother.

117
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:14,080
She won't listen to anything
we say right now.

118
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,240
I'll wait until she's calmed down,

119
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,920
then talk to her again.

120
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,240
Ouch!

121
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:36,360
Mom, I brought some food from Aunt Sa-Ang

122
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,440
so you won't have to cook.

123
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:43,679
-Hey, Mom.
-If you're here to make me sell meatballs,

124
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,840
don't bother. I'm not doing it.

125
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,520
Mom!

126
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:50,480
Your meatball business was doing so well.

127
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:53,960
You use ten kilos of pork a day,
and it all sells out.

128
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:56,040
-If you set up a stall somewhere else,
-Ow! That hurts!

129
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,560
you could sell
through food delivery apps too.

130
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:02,040
You'd get more customers
and make even more money.

131
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,120
Hey!

132
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,040
Mom's hurt this badly,
and you still want her to work, Ob?

133
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,960
-It's all red.
-Let me see.

134
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,400
-Ouch! Be gentle.
-Sorry.

135
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,720
Hello?

136
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:18,880
Yes, speaking.

137
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:20,920
Huh?

138
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,200
Wait a second.

139
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,440
-Just a moment! Hold on.
-What?

140
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,800
Come on. What's going on?

141
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,800
Hello. Is something wrong?

142
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:39,160
Hey! The shoes you sold me are fake.

143
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,800
I've DM'd you on every platform.
Were you ever going to reply?

144
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,920
I had to come all the way to your house.

145
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,560
That's impossible.
All the shoes I sell are authentic.

146
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:48,760
Here, take a look.

147
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:57,160
On authentic shoes, the logo on the sole
should be clearly visible.

148
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:59,760
And the stitching on the shoes you sold me

149
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,040
doesn't match the real ones either. See?

150
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,960
Excuse me. May I take a look?

151
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:16,040
You sold me fake shoes
and passed them off as real, didn't you?

152
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:21,520
No, I only sell authentic shoes.

153
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:24,080
The shop I preordered them from
must've scammed me.

154
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:25,640
Then…

155
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:29,800
I'll refund you first
and order you a new pair.

156
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:33,240
No, thanks. I just want my money back.

157
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,680
Orn!

158
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,720
Orn!

159
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,160
Where did you preorder those shoes?

160
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:00,960
I think we need to report this
to the police.

161
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,880
No need, Auem. I can handle it myself.

162
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,360
-Stay out of it.
-Orn!

163
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:30,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">When will I get my order?</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I paid the deposit a month ago.</font></font></i>

164
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You said it was stuck at customs--</font></font></i>

165
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,280
REMOVE THIS CHAT FROM YOUR INBOX? - REMOVE

166
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,480
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Please refund me for the shoes.</font></font></i>

167
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,000
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you don't refund me or you block me,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I'll go to the police.</font></font></i>

168
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,280
REMOVE THIS CHAT FROM YOUR INBOX? - REMOVE

169
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:57,240
AVAILABLE BALANCE 7,000.79 BAHT

170
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,800
Where am I going to get the money?

171
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,160
Hom Ngern.

172
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:23,560
It's normal for siblings to fight, right?

173
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,840
I wish I could pay off all our debts soon.

174
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,960
Then we wouldn't have to fight
over things like this.

175
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,600
Right?

176
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,560
If you need someone to talk to,

177
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:53,720
you can call me next time.

178
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:58,120
Buffaloes don't talk back
when I talk to them, unlike you.

179
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:03,000
How do you know? Maybe Hom Ngern
talks back to you in her head.

180
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,080
Right, Hom Ngern?

181
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,920
What did you bring? There's so much stuff.

182
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,480
Equipment for growing straw mushrooms.

183
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,480
I'll build you a straw mushroom shed.

184
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:21,720
Did you know the area
around the buffalo pen

185
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:22,960
is perfect for growing straw mushrooms?

186
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,720
-Really?
-Absolutely.

187
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:28,240
There's plenty of straw
and organic manure around the pen.

188
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:31,920
And the humidity is ideal
for mushroom growth.

189
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,200
Plus, you can run this business

190
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,360
alongside the buffalo farm.

191
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,560
It'll give you another source of income.

192
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,120
Aunt Sa-Ang told you about Mom,
didn't she?

193
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:50,720
Auem.

194
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,760
You may lose money,

195
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,680
but don't lose heart.

196
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,800
HOM NGERN

197
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:14,360
Hey, Din! The photos from the shoot
are up on the page.

198
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:16,000
Hom Ngern looks gorgeous.

199
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,000
Hom Ngern, look!

200
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:20,680
You look beautiful! See?

201
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,560
Look how pretty you are, sweetie.

202
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,720
-Wow!
-Let me see.

203
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:30,040
-Look how great these photos are.
-Phet Kla looks great too!

204
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:30,960
PHET KLA

205
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,520
Wow, he's huge.

206
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,640
Do you like it, Hom Ngern?

207
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,080
You're getting famous.

208
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,200
How many likes have we got, Din?

209
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:48,800
-Over a thousand. They were just posted.
-What? Already?

210
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:49,800
Yeah!

211
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,000
So our buffaloes are famous now?

212
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:52,960
Looks like they're getting there.

213
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:58,560
Wow, he's huge!

214
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:01,520
They'd make such a cute couple.

215
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,480
Hom Ngern!

216
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,600
Come on, eat your grass.

217
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,840
Eat up!

218
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:25,880
Yummy?

219
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,520
Huh? Where's Mom's gold?

220
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:52,600
Sure. Just a moment, please.

221
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,200
Let me write down your order first.

222
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:03,040
Of course. Three hundred tubes, right?

223
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,800
Got it. I'll have them ready for you.

224
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,920
Thank you.

225
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:13,600
-Auem.
-Yeah?

226
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:16,680
How much do you charge per dose of semen?

227
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,880
I used to charge 300 baht per dose,

228
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:22,760
but after Phet Kla became champion,
I raised it to 500.

229
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:25,480
Wow, 500 baht a dose!

230
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,480
How many doses till you're rich?

231
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:33,560
A buffalo usually produces
around 300 doses per collection.

232
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:35,800
If I sell them all, that's 150,000 baht.

233
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,080
-Really?
-Yeah.

234
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,600
Auem, someone's here with a delivery.

235
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:48,440
Just a second.

236
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,160
Hello?

237
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,040
Sure.

238
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:33,600
Of course.

239
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,200
How many doses would you like?

240
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:39,280
Okay.

241
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:43,800
Sure, I'll call you
as soon as the semen collection is done.

242
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,280
Okay. Thank you so much.

243
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,320
Bye.

244
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,320
The semen collection's done.
See you next week.

245
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,040
-Thank you, Doctor.
-Thank you.

246
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:17,640
-I'll help carry the stuff to the car.
-Let's go.

247
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,880
Uncle Tik.

248
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,920
People keep asking
if you're selling Por Chang's semen.

249
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:33,600
Are you sure you won't sell any?

250
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,640
I'm really sorry.

251
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:42,360
I'm worried Sia Aun
might secretly send someone to buy it.

252
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:48,440
And you two
shouldn't just sell collected semen.

253
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:51,200
Let your buffaloes
mate naturally sometimes.

254
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:52,800
It'll keep their semen healthy

255
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:55,520
and help improve the bloodline naturally.

256
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:59,280
Auem and I have talked
about offering natural breeding services,

257
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:03,200
but we wanted to ask you
how much we should charge.

258
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:07,040
I also want to find a breeding bull
for Hom Ngern,

259
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:10,040
so we'll have more buffaloes
when we open the conservation center.

260
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,840
Din suggested breeding her with Phet Kla.

261
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,360
What do you think?

262
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:24,680
We can discuss those details later.

263
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,000
Din, go put the semen away.

264
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,480
Okay, Uncle.

265
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,120
Hello.

266
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,720
The semen you ordered is ready.

267
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:17,000
Okay. I'll bring it over right away.

268
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:00,040
I wanted to see how the semen is stored,
so I snuck in to take a look.

269
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:02,800
Don't lie to me.

270
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,080
I know you took a customer's call

271
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:07,120
and planned to sell
Phet Kla's semen yourself.

272
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:14,880
Hello? Sure.

273
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:17,160
How many doses would you like?

274
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:21,800
Sure, I'll call you
as soon as the semen collection is done.

275
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:24,360
Okay. Thank you so much.

276
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:25,600
Bye.

277
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:32,640
Orn, listen.

278
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:34,400
Why would you do this?

279
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:36,480
Huh?

280
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:38,680
Are you buying concert tickets again?

281
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,160
What more do you want, Auem?

282
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:45,440
I didn't even take the semen.

283
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:47,920
Orn! How can you say that?

284
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,960
You haven't even apologized to Din.

285
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,520
Sorry.

286
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:53,080
Happy now?

287
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,160
Not yet.

288
00:22:55,840 --> 00:22:57,040
What do you need the money for?

289
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,800
There's a problem
with the shoes you're selling, right?

290
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:08,600
You know stealing is a crime, right?

291
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:10,080
I could press charges against you.

292
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:12,680
Don't threaten me, Din.

293
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,360
I'm not threatening you.

294
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:15,880
I mean it.

295
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:20,680
Now tell me, Orn.
What do you need the money for?

296
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:42,160
POLICE

297
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:45,600
Ob! Auem!

298
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:48,920
Are you here? Ob! Auem!

299
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:52,440
Come on.

300
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,080
What's wrong, Sa-Ing?

301
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,160
Yeah.

302
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,640
What's happened?
Why are the police with you?

303
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:02,920
I can't reach my kids.
None of them are answering my calls.

304
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,600
Are they here?

305
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:05,960
I saw them around here.

306
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:08,360
Orn!

307
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:12,320
Orn! Why did you do this?

308
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:13,680
-Huh?
-Wait, Mom.

309
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:15,240
What's going on?

310
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:17,200
The police came to our house.

311
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:19,680
They want to take Orn to the station.

312
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:21,640
They said she scammed people out of money.

313
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:25,240
Are you Ms. Ornrada Thadamit?

314
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:29,280
More than ten victims
have filed complaints against you

315
00:24:29,360 --> 00:24:32,600
for fraud
and violating the Computer Crime Act

316
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:35,000
by entering false information
into a computer system.

317
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:36,840
Here's your summons.

318
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:39,840
Please come to the station
for questioning.

319
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:46,160
It's not true, is it? Huh?

320
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:57,880
POLICE

321
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:03,560
These are all the victims
waiting for Ornrada.

322
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:06,640
I suggest you talk to them first.

323
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:09,960
If she were legally an adult,

324
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:12,880
we could charge her with fraud right away.

325
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:15,320
But she's still in high school.

326
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:16,800
This could go on her record.

327
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:19,200
I suggest you speak to the victims first.

328
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:21,600
You might be able to reach a settlement.

329
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,400
Okay.

330
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:29,040
Hello.

331
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:31,600
I'm Ornrada's older sister.

332
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,360
I'm Orn's mother.

333
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:36,640
I'm sorry for what my daughter did.

334
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:38,960
Can we talk this over calmly?

335
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,160
Talk calmly?

336
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,880
If you got scammed,
would you be okay with it?

337
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:45,800
Exactly! How did you raise her?
She's going around scamming people.

338
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,760
Scamming people in high school?
What'll she be like when she grows up?

339
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:51,120
Officer, we're not settling this!

340
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,760
-This is fraud!
-You have to take action.

341
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:54,120
Everyone!

342
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,560
Please calm down, everyone.

343
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:57,120
Please, calm down.

344
00:25:57,200 --> 00:26:00,160
Let me talk to my sister first
and find out what happened.

345
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:01,920
She's still in high school.

346
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:03,720
Come on, Orn.

347
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:06,280
-Will we get our money back?
-Who would put up with this?

348
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:07,640
Come here, Orn.

349
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:08,840
Come here. Sit down.

350
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:14,480
Orn, what's going on? Huh?

351
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:23,200
If you don't tell me what happened,
I can't help you sort this out.

352
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:38,840
ONAIRSHOES

353
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:42,640
I set up an Instagram account
to sell fake shoes.

354
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:46,840
I waited for customers to pay,
then spent their money.

355
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:47,800
Huh?

356
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:52,680
Wait. So you're saying

357
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:56,040
you tried to steal the semen
to pay off your debts?

358
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:04,160
How much do you owe altogether?

359
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:08,280
Altogether, it's…

360
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,160
-300,000 baht.
-What?

361
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,280
Three hundred thousand baht?

362
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:19,120
Orn, how could you scam people
out of that much money?

363
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:21,520
What were you thinking?

364
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:24,400
Aren't you afraid of going to jail
and ruining your future, Orn?

365
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:26,600
-Why did you do this?
-Ugh, Mom!

366
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:30,000
As if our family has such a bright future!

367
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:33,440
We're drowning in debt
and have to save every penny.

368
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:36,640
Do you know my friends
can afford to travel abroad

369
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,360
and buy nice things?

370
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:40,880
Why do you have to have
what everyone else has?

371
00:27:40,960 --> 00:27:42,960
Even you want your buffalo back.

372
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:45,440
-That's different, Orn.
-How is it different?

373
00:27:45,520 --> 00:27:48,400
You love buffaloes,
and I love my own life.

374
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:50,280
I just want a good life like my friends.

375
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:52,240
Like when Dad was still here!

376
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:55,760
I want you to have a good life
like when Dad was here too.

377
00:27:56,520 --> 00:28:01,120
But having a good life doesn't mean
you can go around scamming people.

378
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,480
You were wrong this time, Orn.

379
00:28:06,080 --> 00:28:10,040
You need to apologize to every customer
and work out a repayment plan.

380
00:28:11,040 --> 00:28:13,920
Then we'll figure out
how to solve this together.

381
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:20,600
So what are you going to do?
We've all lost money.

382
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:22,040
Can we pay in installments?

383
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:24,120
That's hundreds of thousands of baht.

384
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:26,280
I've been waiting forever.
How can someone so young

385
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,920
act like this?

386
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,040
This is unacceptable.

387
00:28:29,120 --> 00:28:30,640
-She ignored my calls!
-Well…

388
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:32,480
Can everyone please calm down?

389
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:34,200
-Please calm down.
-That's a lot of money!

390
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:36,240
Right now,

391
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:39,080
she realizes what she did was wrong.

392
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:43,040
But we're talking
about quite a large sum of money.

393
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:44,080
Could you at least

394
00:28:44,160 --> 00:28:46,560
let her pay in installments

395
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:49,040
or pay you back gradually?

396
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:52,520
There's really not much else
we can do about this right now.

397
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:54,480
But we borrowed money for this.

398
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,000
-Yeah.
-We've invested so much already.

399
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:58,200
-When will we get paid? Give us a date!
-Yeah!

400
00:28:58,280 --> 00:29:00,640
-How are you going to pay us back?
-You might just run off.

401
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:04,440
-Exactly! We've lost so much money.
-Our customers are waiting.

402
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:07,200
-How is this going to end?
-Please.

403
00:29:07,280 --> 00:29:08,520
Please let us pay in installments.

404
00:29:09,360 --> 00:29:12,480
Please don't press charges
against my sister.

405
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,120
I promise I'll pay you back
in installments.

406
00:29:14,200 --> 00:29:16,600
Please give my sister another chance.

407
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:20,320
-I'm sorry.
-What if we pay interest too?

408
00:30:01,280 --> 00:30:02,360
Here you go.

409
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,120
Everything's settled now.

410
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:09,080
All the victims have agreed
to a mediated settlement.

411
00:30:09,160 --> 00:30:12,600
But if Ornrada fails
to honor the agreement,

412
00:30:12,680 --> 00:30:14,720
she'll face legal action.

413
00:30:23,840 --> 00:30:25,600
Thank you all so much.

414
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:28,600
I'll make sure Orn earns enough
to pay everyone back

415
00:30:28,680 --> 00:30:30,600
within a month.

416
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,600
BOONYOD FARM

417
00:30:44,680 --> 00:30:46,320
Come on, sweetie.

418
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:49,520
Go take a shower.

419
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:52,480
Not yet, Mom.

420
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:54,360
Auem, come on.

421
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:57,720
-We're all tired. Can't we talk tomorrow?
-We're talking now.

422
00:30:58,760 --> 00:31:00,320
Show me your banking app now.

423
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:02,720
I want to see how much
of that money you've got left.

424
00:31:15,320 --> 00:31:16,680
Only 5,000 baht left?

425
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:21,680
Tomorrow, sell everything you bought.

426
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,200
The concert ticket too.

427
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:24,880
Hey.

428
00:31:24,960 --> 00:31:26,720
Even if she sells all that stuff,

429
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:30,360
it won't be enough to pay back
what she owes.

430
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:31,480
I think…

431
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:35,240
You should use your earnings
to help her first.

432
00:31:35,840 --> 00:31:36,720
Mom.

433
00:31:36,800 --> 00:31:39,800
But Auem and I are saving that money
to buy Hom Thong back.

434
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,640
What? You want Orn to go to jail?

435
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:43,560
Huh?

436
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:45,560
Go get the bankbook.

437
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:48,880
I'll withdraw the money tomorrow
to help Orn.

438
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,160
Then we can put this behind us.

439
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:53,760
-Don't, Mom!
-Listen!

440
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:56,720
We only have a month.
How else can we get the money in time?

441
00:31:58,200 --> 00:32:01,840
Help your sister first.
You can always earn more money later.

442
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:03,320
But Orn did something wrong, Mom.

443
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,200
Shouldn't we teach her
to take responsibility?

444
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:07,960
She needs to pay off her own debts.

445
00:32:08,040 --> 00:32:10,200
Keep spoiling her, and she'll do it again.

446
00:32:10,280 --> 00:32:11,680
Are you blaming me now?

447
00:32:11,760 --> 00:32:13,120
That's enough!

448
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,240
If you don't want to help me, then don't!

449
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:21,200
I'm not your favorite sibling anyway.

450
00:32:22,320 --> 00:32:23,440
Orn!

451
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:25,720
How can you say that?

452
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,360
It's true, isn't it?

453
00:32:28,040 --> 00:32:29,560
You never give me anything I ask for.

454
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:31,240
Nothing I do is ever good enough for you.

455
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:34,640
You only love Ob!

456
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:37,200
I'll sort out my own problems.

457
00:32:37,280 --> 00:32:38,840
I don't need your help!

458
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,960
-Orn.
-Orn.

459
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:46,400
Orn.

460
00:33:39,240 --> 00:33:41,160
What should I do, Hom Ngern?

461
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:44,960
I really want to bring Hom Thong
back to you soon.

462
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:48,680
But Orn's my sister too.

463
00:34:17,159 --> 00:34:19,679
DEPOSIT - BALANCE

464
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:34,280
ANIMAL FEED FOR SALE

465
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:38,920
Say goodbye to mosquitoes and insects
bothering your buffaloes.

466
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:42,800
Just use this insect repellent
from Chettha Kaset Farm.

467
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:46,159
It's made entirely
from organic ingredients.

468
00:34:46,239 --> 00:34:49,239
"And we've got a special offer today,
right, Auem?"

469
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:51,320
That's right.

470
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:54,000
Buy five one-liter bottles

471
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:57,560
and get a 500 ml bottle absolutely free.

472
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:05,560
Let's check the comments.

473
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:09,320
Can you show us the free mosquito net?

474
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:11,560
Of course. Let me grab it for you.

475
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:14,240
Here it is.

476
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:18,240
-Ah…
-Auem.

477
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:27,080
This is the free mosquito net.

478
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:30,040
I'll be ending the livestream in an hour.

479
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:39,680
I know you're stressed about Orn,

480
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:42,240
but you need to take care
of yourself too. Okay?

481
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,880
What am I supposed to do?

482
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:46,800
I can't eat.

483
00:35:46,880 --> 00:35:48,920
I didn't sleep a wink last night.

484
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:52,120
If I use the money saved for Hom Thong
to help Orn,

485
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:53,840
I'll feel bad for Ob.

486
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:55,480
But if I don't help Orn,

487
00:35:56,120 --> 00:35:58,000
I'll feel guilty.

488
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,400
What should I do, Din?

489
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:03,360
When will Mom and Orn understand

490
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:05,640
that things aren't the way
they used to be?

491
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:08,080
Listen, Auem.

492
00:36:10,080 --> 00:36:13,280
Everyone adjusts to problems
at their own pace.

493
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:16,560
Maybe you need to give them
a little more time.

494
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:20,720
And how much longer is a little?

495
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:22,440
I don't know either.

496
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:25,720
But you have to understand.
Uncle Yod always took care of them.

497
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:29,040
You can't expect them
to change in just a month or two.

498
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:31,080
It's like raising buffaloes.

499
00:36:31,160 --> 00:36:34,080
Each one has a different personality.

500
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:36,760
Remember when Uncle Tik
had you lead Por Chang

501
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:39,760
and Phet Kla? You used
different techniques for each.

502
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:41,080
Right?

503
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:43,680
But there's one thing

504
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:46,720
that helped you win them over.

505
00:36:50,080 --> 00:36:53,000
-Treating them with love?
-Exactly!

506
00:36:53,080 --> 00:36:55,720
If you want Aunt Sa-Ing and Orn
to understand you,

507
00:36:55,800 --> 00:36:57,640
you need to understand them too.

508
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:58,640
Right?

509
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:04,520
Wow.

510
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:05,840
I never thought

511
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:08,960
I'd hear something so wise
coming from you.

512
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:11,720
Wise words aren't all I've got.

513
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,160
I've got sweet words too.

514
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:15,720
Oh, please!

515
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:17,560
I'm going to help Rung.

516
00:37:17,640 --> 00:37:18,640
Wait.

517
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:23,600
I want you to know something.

518
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:27,080
No matter how many problems come your way,

519
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,240
I'll always be by your side.

520
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,680
This buffalo boy right here

521
00:37:32,760 --> 00:37:34,040
will always look after you.

522
00:37:38,280 --> 00:37:40,360
-Want another one?
-That's enough.

523
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:42,760
Jak!

524
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:45,000
I'm returning the products
from the livestream.

525
00:37:45,720 --> 00:37:47,960
Okay. Let's see.

526
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:49,040
Everything here?

527
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:51,960
All here.

528
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:54,920
Please sign to confirm the return.

529
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:55,840
Okay.

530
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:58,080
-Here.
-Alright.

531
00:37:58,160 --> 00:37:59,920
Should I take these to the warehouse?

532
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:02,480
No, it's okay. I'll put them away myself.

533
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:04,720
I'll come pick them up again
for the next livestream.

534
00:38:04,800 --> 00:38:05,680
Okay. See you.

535
00:38:05,760 --> 00:38:07,320
-Thanks.
-Let's go.

536
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:21,600
CHETTHA KASET FARM

537
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,840
CHETTHA KASET FARM

538
